{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head 958d4a3f53114eec60d8e08b9371400f8a84119e on builder/sh1-self-host-screens-20261117, the SH-1 design note, for request 2d48b0e5 under my promise f3e915b8. The implementation is SH-1 (request e59cdd5f, promise 943a5234). This approval covers the design only.\n\nThe head has one path, notes/2026-11-17-sh1-self-host-screens.md, so it needs no gate under GS-1. `git merge-tree --write-tree 69b85e98 958d4a3f` merges cleanly to tree f74e8bb2. check-notes gives 0 warnings. The commit-message check passes with 2 checked and 0 flagged, and `git diff --check` is clean.\n\nI read the diff from 1549f891, which answers each change in my verdict 5302df93:\n\n1. Host dispatch. Section 2 step 1 now sends only the host of `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the room `fetch` and a descriptor's hostname to the sandbox handler. Every other host gets 404. The note states that the room page never answers on a screen name, in any configuration state, and names owner steps 4 to 10 and a redeploy from an old project directory. The planned workerd test adds an unknown host and a screen name with no deployed setting, each answering 404 on `/` and on the room page path.\n2. Descriptor rule. On an `inguz.space` origin, every answer other than a valid 200 fails closed, 404 included, as `application-screen.ts:25-30` does today. Only another origin keeps the 404 same-origin path. The planned tests add the refused 404 on `inguz.space`.\n3. Same site. Section 3 states that `screens.room.example` and the room are same-site, that screen script can set a cookie the room receives, and that the room reads no cookie at c17d556d. The source head adds a no-cookie pin to `security-entry-points.test.mjs`.\n\nFor the source head, I will check these points:\n\n- The dispatch compares hosts exactly: case-folded and without a port, so a `Host` such as `ROOM.EXAMPLE:443` neither reaches the wrong handler nor fails a valid request.\n- The no-cookie pin covers room, scope and client source